# Code-coverage instrumentation scope for the Track-B (commercial fabric IP) builds.
#
# Project scope decision (2026-08-02): the VIP verifies up to the fabric
# INTERFACE only. The commercial fabric IP internals are licensed third-party
# IP, delivered pre-verified, and are golden here (project iron rule 1:
# never patch ext/). Leaving them instrumented put ~300 .v files of ARM RTL in
# the code-coverage denominator, which is neither our verification target nor
# something our stimulus is meant to close -- it just deflated LINE/TOGGLE and
# made the VIP's own numbers unreadable.
#
# What stays instrumented:
#   hdl_top                      - clock/reset, the VIP<->fabric wiring block
#   u_fabric_ip     - axi4_fabric_ip_wrapper, the vectorised interface
#                      adapter we wrote and DO own
#   the whole VIP (agents, env, bfm interfaces)
# What is excluded:
#   u_fabric_ip.u_fabric - the generated fabric IP itself (ASIBs, AMIBs,
#                          busmatrix, arbiters, CDC, default slave)
#
# Usage: vcs ... -cm_hier ../../sim/coverage_scope.cm_hier
+tree hdl_top
-tree hdl_top.u_fabric_ip.u_fabric
